p.seg:
—ἑαυτοῦ
								would be more correct here and in c. 3.4;
								but the whole side is meant.

—Steph. Byz. says Philistus
								referred to it as φρούριον Σικελίας;
								but it is quite unknown.

—i.e. the other Aegean islands;
								it was their duty to supply πεζὸν καὶ
									χρήματα.

—observe that Thuc. uses the
								earlier form of the augment whenever there are two ways of
								angmenting a verb: e.g. χρῆν, not ἐχρῆν;
									καθῖζον, not ἐκάθιζον;
								ἑνηντιούμην, not ἠναντιούμην;
								see Rutherford New Phryn. p. 81; and for the
								Attic uses of καθίζω
									ib. p. 336.

]—to be omitted,
								since there is no contrast between the doings of Greeks and of other
								men.
